{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>On the tenth the tops of the mountains were seen.</b> This is Av, which is the tenth of Marcheshvan, when the rain began. And if you would say it is Elul, and the tenth of Kislev, when the rain ceased — just as you say ״in the seventh month,״ Sivan, which is seventh to the cessation — it is impossible to say so; perforce you count ״seventh״ only to the cessation, since the forty days of the rains' descent, and the hundred and fifty of the waters' surging, did not end until the first of Sivan. And if you say ״seventh״ to the descent, this is not Sivan; and the ״tenth״ cannot be counted except to the descent — for if you say to the cessation and it is Elul, you will not find that on the first of the first month the waters had dried from the earth. For at the end of forty days from when the tops of the mountains were seen he sent the raven, and twenty-one days he waited while sending the dove — that makes sixty days from when the tops of the mountains were seen until the face of the ground dried. And if you say they were seen in Elul, it turns out they dried in Marcheshvan, and he calls it ״the first״ — and that can only be Tishrei, which is first to the creation of the world; and according to Rabbi Yehoshua it is Nisan."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:57.792746951Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}